    "Curve2": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A baseline. Arcs stay arcs; chording is a BUILD-time choice at a stated sagitta, never a READ-time loss. cad.py:200 skips ARC today only because it had nowhere to put one. LWPOLYLINE bulges MUST be read with e.get_points('xyb') — get_points('xy') is the single commonest way a curved wall silently becomes a straight one.",
